# SoutNaqi Rules

Follow this entire document whenever working on this project. Satellite rule files in `.cursor/rules/` provide additional details for specific areas.

---

## 1. Project Overview

Bilingual (Arabic / English) Flutter application for audio and video processing: trimming, transcoding, vocal/source separation, waveform visualization, and project history.

- **Package**: `soutnaqi`
- **State Management**: `flutter_bloc` (Cubits) + `Equatable`
- **Media Processing**: FFmpeg on IO platforms; stubs on Web
- **UI Framework**: Material 3, `hugeicons`, `google_fonts`
- **Strict Rule**: Do NOT introduce GetX, Riverpod, or Provider.

---

## 2. Architecture & File Structure

```
lib/features/<feature>/{cubit,data,ui}
lib/core/{theme,widgets,config,errors,logging,toast,layout,constants}
lib/l10n/
```

- **Feature-first**: Every new feature lives inside its own folder under `lib/features/<feature>/`.
- **Core Widgets**: Place widgets in `lib/core/widgets/` ONLY when shared across multiple features.
- **Imports**: Always use absolute package imports: `package:soutnaqi/...`.
- **Platform Separation**: Pair `*_platform.dart` with `*_io.dart` and `*_stub.dart`.
- **Clean UI**: Never execute FFmpeg commands, direct IO, or business logic inside `ui/` files.

---

## 3. Dart & Engineering Quality

- Use `const` constructors wherever possible and declare `super.key`.
- State classes: Extend `Equatable` and implement `copyWith`. Mark private fields with `_`.
- Logging: Never use raw `print()`. Use `appLog.d`, `appLog.i`, `appLog.w`, or `appLog.e`.
- Colors: Always obtain colors via `context.accentPrimary` and semantic tokens. Never hardcode `Color(0xFF...)` in UI widgets.
- Icons: Use `HugeIconsStrokeRounded.*`.
- Strings: Retrieve all UI text from `AppLocalizations.of(context)` exclusively.
- Verification: Always verify UI modifications in both Light and Dark modes, and in RTL (Arabic) and LTR (English).

---

## 4. Brand & Identity

- **Name**: SoutNaqi / صوت نقي.
- **Brand Mark**: Clean white waveform on a `#2563EB` rounded square.
- **Tokens**: Use `MaglissColorTokens` (legacy `Magliss*` naming is preserved for design continuity).
- **Color Palette**: Primary Blue `#2563EB`, Violet `#7C3AED`, Light Background `#F4F6FA`, Dark Background `#0B0F17`.
- **Logo**: Use `SoutNaqiLogo` exclusively.
- **Contrast**: For text over accent surfaces, use `context.onAccent`.
- **Typography**: Cairo font for Arabic, Inter font for English, accessed via `font*W*` helpers.
- **Corner Radii**: Use `AppRadii` constants (`sm: 8`, `md: 12`, `lg: 16`, `xl: 20`).

---

## 5. Localization (l10n)

- Template files: `lib/l10n/app_en.arb` and `lib/l10n/app_ar.arb`. Every key must exist in both files.
- Domain Errors: Map errors via `AppException.messageKey` to localized strings via `appExceptionMessage`.
- String Construction: Never concatenate localized words or sentences. Always define placeholders in the ARB files.

---

## 6. State Management

- Use a single Cubit per feature screen/flow.
- Always emit a new state instance after processing results.
- Wrap background fire-and-forget tasks (e.g. project history indexing, temp file cleanup) in `unawaited(...)`.
- Throw typed `AppException` instances from data sources/repositories, and handle them in the UI with `AppToast`.

---

## 7. Platform Separation & Web Stubs

```dart
import 'service_stub.dart'
    if (dart.library.io) 'service_io.dart';
```

- Web support: Return `isProcessingSupported == false` and present `processingWebUnsupported` message.
- Zero IO on Web: Never import `dart:io` outside of `*_io.dart` files.
- Completeness: Every processing or native operation must implement both IO and Stub versions.

---

## 8. Errors & User Feedback

- Never display raw technical error strings (`error.toString()`) to the user.
- Adding a new error: Add key to usage site + `app_en.arb` + `app_ar.arb` + `app_exception_l10n.dart`.
- Feedback Toasts: Use `AppToast.showLoading`, `AppToast.showSuccess`, and `AppToast.showFailure`.

---

## 9. Layout & Screen Adaptability

- **Responsive Breakpoint**: Screen width >= 800dp displays the desktop/tablet sidebar; width < 800dp displays UniversalAppBar + `ShellBottomNav`.
- **Safe Padding**: Apply `maglissShellScrollPadding` and `maglissBottomNavPadding`.
- **Shell Tabs**: `workspace`, `history`, `settings`. The default tab is `workspace`. No separate `home` tab.
- **App Bar**: On mobile, avoid repeating the tab title in the page body if the AppBar already displays it.

---

## 10. Android & Google Play Release Rules

### 10.1. Photo & Video Permissions Policy (Strict Compliance)
- **Zero Broad Media Permissions**: NEVER declare `READ_MEDIA_IMAGES` or `READ_MEDIA_VIDEO` in `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml`. Google Play restricts these permissions exclusively to core gallery/device-manager apps and rejects standard media-processing apps that declare them.
- **System Photo Picker**: Always use the modern Android Photo Picker via `image_picker` (`ImagePicker().pickVideo(source: ImageSource.gallery)`), which requires **zero permissions** on Android 13+ (API 33+).
- **Audio Document Picker**: For audio files, always use Storage Access Framework (SAF) document picking via `file_picker` (`ACTION_OPEN_DOCUMENT`), which grants temporary URI read access without requiring broad media declarations.
- **Legacy Android**: On Android 12 and below (API <= 32), storage access is covered by `READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` with `android:maxSdkVersion="32"`.
- **Queries Declaration**: Always maintain system picker intents (`GET_CONTENT`, `OPEN_DOCUMENT`, `CHOOSER`, `PICK`) in the `<queries>` block of `AndroidManifest.xml` for package visibility on Android 11+ (API 30+).

### 10.2. Release Builds & Minification (R8)
- **R8 Optimization & Obfuscation Enabled**: Keep `isMinifyEnabled = true` and `isShrinkResources = true` with `proguard-android-optimize.txt` in `android/app/build.gradle.kts` to satisfy Google Play Console's DEX code optimization and obfuscation threshold (>= 25%).
- **Targeted ProGuard Keep Rules**: In `android/app/proguard-rules.pro`, keep Flutter/JNI/plugin entrypoints (`io.flutter.**`, `io.flutter.plugins.**`, `com.arthenica.ffmpegkit.**`, `ai.onnxruntime.**`, `com.mr.flutter.plugin.filepicker.**`, `com.miguelruivo.flutter.plugin.filepicker.**`) and targeted reflection/protobuf/atomic members (`androidx.datastore.preferences.PreferencesProto**`, `GeneratedMessageLite` members, `kotlinx.coroutines.**` volatile fields, `androidx.lifecycle.DefaultLifecycleObserver`). Never put blanket `-keep class` on large AndroidX/KotlinX packages (`androidx.media3.**`, `androidx.datastore.**`, `kotlinx.coroutines.**`), as that prevents R8 from obfuscating most of the DEX and drops obfuscation below Google Play's 25% requirement.

### 10.3. Native Debug Symbols & Deobfuscation
- **Native Debug Symbols**: Always specify `ndk { debugSymbolLevel = "SYMBOL_TABLE" }` in `buildTypes.release` in `android/app/build.gradle.kts`. This packages native C/C++ debug symbol tables (for FFmpeg, ONNX Runtime, and the Flutter engine) directly into the App Bundle (`.aab`), completely eliminating the missing debug symbols warning in Google Play Console.

### 10.4. 16 KB Page Size & NDK Compatibility
- **NDK r28+ Enforcement**: Keep `ndkVersion = "28.2.13676358"` (NDK r28c+) in `android/app/build.gradle.kts` and `android/build.gradle.kts` so all native libraries are compiled with 16 KB page-size runtime support.
- **Exclude Legacy DataStore Native Counter**: Always exclude `**/libdatastore_shared_counter.so` under `packaging.jniLibs.excludes` in `android/app/build.gradle.kts`. That library is shipped prebuilt with an older NDK (`r25c`) inside `androidx.datastore:datastore-core-android`, is only used by `MultiProcessDataStoreFactory` (never loaded by single-process `shared_preferences_android`), and triggers Google Play Console's 16 KB older-NDK crash warning if packaged.

